A simple fortran code to concatenate a list of (ASCII) files into a sh-separable single file (like a tarball).
Interactive, text-menu driven, self-explanatory.
The filecat.input file illustrates how this code would create a file "utils.sh"
that contains a series of fortran files within this utils directory, through the following:

filecat << filecat.input

filecat.input:
utils.sh
birch.f
bonds.f
cells.f
config.f
emin.f
filecat.f
mk_hcp.f
mktape5.f
outpost.f
qgrids.f
rings.f
quit

